  "name": "TLC DLC",
  "code": "TLDLC",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"390\" data-end=\"524\">\n<p data-start=\"392\" data-end=\"524\"><strong data-start=\"392\" data-end=\"423\">Total Leukocyte Count (TLC)</strong> indicates the total number of white blood cells and helps identify infections or immune disorders.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"525\" data-end=\"710\">\n<p data-start=\"527\" data-end=\"710\"><strong data-start=\"527\" data-end=\"565\">Differential Leukocyte Count (DLC)</strong> provides the percentage of different types of white blood cells to help differentiate between bacterial, viral, allergic, or parasitic causes.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Parameter</th>\n<th>Interpretation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total Leukocyte Count (TLC)</strong></td>\n<td>High TLC (leukocytosis) suggests infection, inflammation, or stress response. Low TLC (leukopenia) may occur in viral infections, bone marrow suppression, or certain medications.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Neutrophils</strong></td>\n<td>Increased in bacterial infections, stress, or inflammation. Decreased in viral infections or bone marrow suppression.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Lymphocytes</strong></td>\n<td>Increased in viral infections and lymphocytic leukemia. Decreased in stress, corticosteroid use, or immunodeficiency.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Eosinophils</strong></td>\n<td>Increased in allergic reactions, asthma, and parasitic infections.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Monocytes</strong></td>\n<td>Increased in chronic infections such as tuberculosis or inflammatory conditions.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Basophils</strong></td>\n<td>Increased in allergic reactions, myeloproliferative disorders, or chronic inflammation.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
